window.KB_BODY[29]={"tsb101058":"<h2>New KV Lubrication Oil Filter Head Gasket</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/lf6hdha.png\" alt=\"lf6hdha.png\"></figure><p>This document announces the release of a new lubricating oil filter head gasket for use on K38, K50, QSK38, and QSK50 series engines built with inboard piston cooling nozzles. The gasket material has been changed from steel core to edge molded to increase durability and to improve engine reliability. The new edge molded gasket is used for both the inlet and outlet port connections of the lubricating oil filter head.</p><p>Engines built with outboard piston cooling nozzles can <b>not</b> use the new edge molded gasket and <b>must</b> use the old steel core gaskets for the inlet (1) and outlet (2) connections of the lubricating oil filter head. This is due to the oil supply for the outboard piston cooling nozzles coming through the outlet port of the lubricating oil filter head.</p><p>Since engines built with outboard cooling nozzles still require the steel core gaskets, they will continue to be available for service.</p><p>Use the following procedures for information on the lubricating filter head and gasket installation in the K38, K50, QSK38, and QSK50 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021528\">4021528</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/28-007-015-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-015 in Section 7.</a> <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/28-007-067-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-067 in Section 7.</a></p><p>The effective date for implementation into production for all K38, K50, QSK38, and QSK50 engines is as follows:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Engine Plant</th><th>Implementation Date</th><th>ESN First</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Daventry</td><td>18 October, 2010</td><td>33183482</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Table 2: Piston Cooling Nozzle Part Numbers</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th></th><th>Outboard Piston Cooling Nozzles</th><th>Inboard Piston Cooling Nozzles</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>Item No.</b></td><td><b>Description</b></td><td><b>Old Part Number</b></td><td><b>Material</b></td><td><b>Quantity</b></td><td><b>New Part Number</b></td><td><b>Material</b></td><td><b>Quantity</b></td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Gasket</td><td>3629387</td><td>Steel Core</td><td>1</td><td>3643837</td><td>Edge Molded</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Gasket</td><td>3177108</td><td>Steel Core</td><td>1</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb101061":"<h2>QST30 Piston Ring Set - Top Compression Ring Change for Service</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Technical Service Bulletin informs the field that a new top compression piston ring is being used in the QST30 piston ring set, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3804708\">3804708</a>. This top compression piston ring change is for service <b>only</b>. Factory installed top compression piston rings will remain unchanged. The switch from the old to new top compression piston ring in the service kits began between June and September 2010. The piston ring set part number will <b>not</b> be changing. See Table 1 for changes to piston rings used in production and service.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th></th><th><b>New Service Part Number</b></th><th><b>Old Service Part Number</b></th><th><b>Production Part Number</b></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Piston Ring Set</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3804708\">3804708</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3804708\">3804708</a></td><td>N/A</td></tr><tr><td>Top Compression Ring</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4975767\">4975767</a> marked as 1RX</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092569\">3092569</a> Marked as 1R</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092569\">3092569</a> Marked as 1R</td></tr><tr><td>Second Compression Ring</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092570\">3092570</a> Marked as 2RN</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092570\">3092570</a> Marked as 2RN</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092570\">3092570</a> Marked as 2RN</td></tr><tr><td>Oil Piston Ring</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092571\">3092571</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092571\">3092571</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092571\">3092571</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The two different top compression rings are interchangeable, but can be identified by the difference in appearance. The new service top compression piston ring has a white paint mark and the top compression piston ring installed from the factory has an orange color paint mark. The two top compression rings also have different profiles that are shown in Figure 1.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01l00005.png\" alt=\"01l00005.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1. Profile of New Service Top Compression Piston Ring (left) and Profile of Factory Installed Top Compression Piston Ring and Old Service Top Compression Piston Ring (right).</p><p>Different markings appear on the two top compression rings. The top compression ring used for service (1) is marked with “1RX” and the top compression piston ring formerly used for service and presently installed in the factory (2) is marked with “1R” on one side of the end gap and “A” on the other side. These markings are shown in Figure 2.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01l00007.png\" alt=\"01l00007.png\"></figure><p>Figure 2.</p><p>Figure 2. Locations of distinguishing markings on both top compression piston rings.</p><p>When installing all piston rings, make sure the identification markings are facing up.</p><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb101088":"<h2>Crankshaft and Accessory Drive Seals</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This document introduces an updated list for the rotating shaft oil seals, dust seals (POSE), and installation/service tools that are available for the engines listed in the following tables.</p><p>Definition of Terms Used in this Topic</p><p>Production Seal</p><p>The production seal is the base seal used in new production engine build. In production, mounting parts are structured with the seal for installation on the assembly line. The mounting parts can include o-rings, gaskets, capscrews, and so forth. A production seal expander (a special tool, <b>not</b> a plastic or metal ring) is also used when the seal is installed over the shaft. This prevents damage to the sealing element during installation.</p><p>In cases where mounting parts or seal expanders are <b>not</b> required (pressed-in bore seals/shaft installed through the seal), the production seal is also released for service.</p><p>Service Seal with Installation Sleeve</p><p>The service seal includes a disposable sleeve for installations where the seal <b>must</b> be installed over the shaft. The service seal is shipped with the seal installed on the installation sleeve. The seal <b>must not</b> be removed from the installation sleeve prior to seal installation. During installation, the seal and sleeve are positioned on the end of the shaft as an assembly. The seal is then pushed off the installation sleeve and onto the shaft. The installation sleeve is then removed, and the appropriate seal installation tool is used to push the seal into the seal bore or to seat the seal against the housing, depending on the application.</p><p>Service Seal Assembly with Wear Sleeve</p><p>The service seal with wear sleeve was developed for use where the shaft sealing surface has been severely worn or damaged. The wear sleeve is 1.57-mm [0.062-in] thick to provide a robust wear surface for the seal. The seal used with the wear sleeve was designed specifically for use with the 1.57-mm [0.062-in] thick wear sleeve. The seal is <b>not</b> interchangeable with the standard production or service seal since it has a larger inside diameter and fits <b>only</b> the thick-wall wear sleeve. If either the wear sleeve or seal is replaced, or the seal is removed, the complete seal and wear sleeve assembly <b>must</b> be replaced.</p><p>The press-fit wear sleeve and seal assembly <b>must</b> be installed in one operation. The installation requires the use of a special service tool that was designed specifically to install the seal assembly. Refer to the engine model and seal position in this topic to determine the service tool required to install the service seal with wear sleeve. The assembly <b>can not</b> be installed on the shaft without the special installation service tool.</p><p>The service seal with wear sleeve assembly is <b>not</b> available for all engine models or seal positions included in this topic. <b>Only</b> those listed in this topic under each specific engine model and seal position are available at this time.</p><p>Positive-on-Shaft Excluder (POSE)</p><p>The POSE seal was developed to improve primary seal durability. The POSE seal is installed in front of the primary seal and rotates with the shaft. The POSE seal was developed to improve primary seal durability. The POSE seal is installed in front of the primary seal and rotates with the shaft, which reduces the amount of dirt reaching the primary sealing element. This significantly increases seal life, especially in applications in which the seal is exposed to a highly abrasive environment. The POSE seal was designed to be used in conjunction with standard oil seals. No special service tools are required to install the POSE seal. The POSE seal can be installed onto the shaft using <b>only</b> hand-pressure.</p><p>The POSE seal is <b>not</b> available for all engine models or seal positions included in this topic. <b>Only</b> those listed in this topic under each specific engine model and seal position are available at this time.</p><p>Service Tool for Service Seal Installation</p><p>The service tools developed for installation of the standard service seal in some cases are multipurpose, and can also be used to remove the seal. The tools are designed to install the service seal properly to the correct depth in the seal bore without damaging the sealing element, shaft, or seal bore. It is recommended that the proper service tool be used anytime seal replacement is required. Attempting to install the service seal without the proper installation tool can result in seal, shaft, or bore damage that will progress into oil leaks.</p><p>Service Tool for Installation of Service Seal with Wear Sleeve</p><p>This service tool is designed specifically for installation of the service seal with wear sleeve. The service seal and 1.57-mm [0.060-in] thick wear sleeve are available <b>only</b> as an assembly and can be installed <b>only</b> by using the proper service tool. The sleeve and wear sleeve assembly <b>must not</b> be disassembled for any reason during the installation process. Removal of the seal from the wear sleeve will result in seal damage; the seal can <b>not</b> be reinstalled on the wear sleeve without damaging the sealing lip.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> attempt to install the seal/wear sleeve without the proper service tool.</p><p>Repair Sleeve 0.304-mm [0.012-in thick]</p><p>The 0.304-mm [0.012-in] thick repair sleeve, commonly referred to as the “speedi sleeve,” has been used with limited success for several years. The repair sleeve was designed for use on rotating shafts that had experienced minor wear in the seal contact area. A standard service seal is used in conjunction with the repair sleeve. The use of a standard service seal on the thin-walled repair sleeve increases seal-lip loading, which occasionally results in seal failure because of extreme temperatures generated by the friction between the seal lip and the repair sleeve.</p><p>Installation of the thin-wall wear sleeve is also extremely critical because of the wall&#x27;s thickness. Any distortion of the repair sleeve during installation will result in oil leakage between the sleeve and shaft. The working environment of the engine <b>must</b> also be considered when using the repair sleeve. The service life of the repair sleeve is extremely limited in highly abrasive environments because of the wall thickness of the repair sleeve.</p><p>The 0.034-mm [0.012-in] thick repair sleeve is considered a temporary repair <b>only</b> and <b>must</b> be used with discretion. Cummins has obsoleted some of these repair sleeves because of poor performance in the field. These thin-walled repair sleeves are being replaced with the service seal wear sleeve.</p><p>Unitized Seals</p><p>Unitized (one-piece) accessory drive and crankshaft seals were introduced with the release of the QSK19 engine. The unitized seal kits released for service of the QSK19 contain a disposable plastic installation tool. The tool <b>must</b> be used to install the service seal. The seal is <b>not</b> available for service without the tool.</p><p>The unitized seals are also used on the QSK45/60 engines; however, the installation tool is <b>not</b> included with the service seal. The accessory drive seals do <b>not</b> require an installation tool. The seal is pressed into position during installation of the accessory drive pulley. The front and rear crankshaft seal do require an installation tool. Reference the QSK45/60 service tools in this document for the correct crankshaft seal installation tool.</p><p>The unitized seal provides improved durability over the previous conventional-design seals.</p><p>special instructions for K19/QSK19 Rear Crankshaft Seals</p><p>Crankshaft Standardization</p><p>A new high-wall crankshaft (material added in area of rod pin to make sidewalls higher), Part Number 3096362 (bare crankshaft), was released into production and service for both K19/QSK19 construction and marine engines in May 1997. The crankshaft was released for generator set engines in October 1997. The rear crankshaft seal area of the crankshaft, Part Number 3096362, is 0.020-inch larger in diameter, 152.908 mm versus 152.4 mm [6.020 inches versus 6 inches], than the crankshaft, Part Number 201082, previously used in the K19 engine. The increased diameter was required to accommodate the use of the unitized seal for the QSK19 engine.</p><p>When replacing the rear crankshaft seal on K19 engines built or upfitted in the field with crankshaft, Part Number 3096362 (identified by 0.254-mm [0.010-in] step between the flywheel pivot and seal area once the seal is removed). Use either the standard K19 service seal, Part Number 3870890 (dry), or unitized QSK19 seal, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3804704\">3804704</a> (dry), can be used; however, the unitized seal is recommended because of improved seal durability.</p><p>When replacing the rear seal on wet-housing applications using crankshaft, Part Number 3096362, the service rear seal, Part Number 3090297, <b>must</b> be used on both K19 and QSK19 engines. This seal includes a wear sleeve that is designed to accommodate the 0.254-mm [0.010-in] step in the crankshaft seal area.</p><p>Rear Gear Drive Crankshaft</p><p>To date, all QSK19 rear gear drive engines have been built with the standard K19 rear gear drive crankshaft, Part Number 3016098 (bare crankshaft). When replacing the rear crankshaft seal on QSK19 engines built with the crankshaft, Part Number 3016098, the standard K19 rear seal, Part Number 3005886 (wet), or crankshaft, Part Number 3870890 (dry), <b>must</b> be used.</p><p>The crankshaft, Part Number 3016098, has been superseded by high-sidewall crankshaft, Part Number 3331587 (bare crankshaft), for both the K19 and QSK19 rear gear drive engines. The rear seal area of the crankshaft, Part Number 3331587, is 0.508-mm [0.020-in] larger in diameter, 152.908 mm versus 152.4 mm [6.020 inches versus 6.000 inches], than the crankshaft, Part Number 3016098, previously used on K19 and QSK19 rear gear drive engines.</p><p>The crankshaft, Part Number 3331587, can be identified once the rear seal is removed by the 0.254-mm [ 0.010-in] step between the flywheel pilot diameter and the seal area.</p><p>When replacing the rear crankshaft seal on the rear gear drive engines built with or upfitted with the high-wall crankshaft, Part Number 3331587, it is recommended that the QSK19 unitized rear seal, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3804704\">3804704</a> (dry), be used because of improved seal durability.</p><p>When replacing the rear seal on <b>wet-housing</b> applications using the crankshaft, Part Number 3331587, service rear seal, Part Number 3090297 (nonunitized seal), <b>must</b> be used on both the K19 and QSK19 engines. This seal includes a wear sleeve that is designed to accommodate the 0.254-mm [0.010-in] step in the crankshaft seal area.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th><b>Seal Location</b></th><th><b>Production Seal Part Number</b></th><th><b>Service Seal with Installtion Sleeve Part Number (if required)</b></th><th><b>Service Seal Assembly with Wear Sleeve Part Number</b></th><th><b>Pose Excluder</b></th><th><b>Service Tool for Service Seal Part Number</b></th><th><b>Service Tool for Service Seal with Wear Sleeve Part Number</b></th><th><b>Repair Sleeve (Thin-Wall 0.012-Inch)</b></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>V378/504 Engines (Right-Hand Rotation)</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Front Crankshaft Seal</td><td>212227</td><td>3010457</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST971</td><td>-</td><td>3010464</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Dry)</td><td>3010458</td><td>3010459</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST972</td><td>-</td><td>3010465</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Wet)</td><td>3275373</td><td>3008575</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST972</td><td>-</td><td>3010465</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive</td><td>140896</td><td>106276</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td><b>V378/504 Engines (Left-Hand Rotation)</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Front Crankshaft Seal</td><td>3010462</td><td>3010461</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST971</td><td>-</td><td>3010464</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Dry)</td><td>3010460</td><td>3010461</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST972</td><td>-</td><td>3010465</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Wet)</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive</td><td>210764</td><td>106276</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td><b>V/VT555 Engine (Right-Hand Rotation)</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Front Crankshaft Seal</td><td>3010460</td><td>3013461</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST1302</td><td>-</td><td>3010465</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Dry)</td><td>3010458</td><td>3010459</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST1302</td><td>-</td><td>3010465</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Wet)</td><td>3275373</td><td>3008575</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>3010465</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive</td><td>210764</td><td>106276</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td><b>V/VT555 Engine (Left-Hand Rotation)</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Front Crankshaft Seal</td><td>3010458</td><td>3010459</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST1302</td><td>-</td><td>3010465</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Dry)</td><td>3010460</td><td>3010461</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST1302</td><td>-</td><td>3010465</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Wet)</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive</td><td>210764</td><td>106276</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td><b>VT-8-370 Marine (Left-Hand Rotation)</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Front Crankshaft Seal (Left-Hand Rotation)</td><td>3021093</td><td>3021094</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST1071</td><td>-</td><td>3006740</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Dry)</td><td>3013347</td><td>3013347</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST1108</td><td>-</td><td>3006741</td></tr><tr><td><b>V/VT903 Engines</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Front Crankshaft Seal</td><td>3020191</td><td>3020184</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST1071</td><td>-</td><td>3006740</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Dry)</td><td>218539</td><td>218539</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST1108</td><td>-</td><td>3006741</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Wet)</td><td>3002356</td><td>3002356</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>3375818</td><td>-</td><td>3006741</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive</td><td>3020187</td><td>3020187</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td><b>VT903 Bus Engines (Left-Hand Rotation)</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Front Crankshaft Seal</td><td>3021093</td><td>3021094</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST1071</td><td>-</td><td>3006740</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Dry)</td><td>3016660</td><td>3016660</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST1108</td><td>-</td><td>3006741</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Wet)</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td><b>K19 Engines</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Front Crankshaft Seal</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3016787\">3016787</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3016792\">3016792</a>*</td><td>3803994</td><td>3331663</td><td>3824760</td><td>3824760</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Dry)</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4922217\">4922217</a></td><td>3870890</td><td>3099421</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>3824971</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Wet)</td><td>3005883</td><td>3005886</td><td>3090298</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>3824971</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive(Fuel-Pump Side)</td><td>362889</td><td>3628895</td><td>3803852</td><td>3628894</td><td>3824922</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive (Water-Pump Side)</td><td>3016791</td><td>3016794</td><td>-</td><td>3169024</td><td>3824922</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td><b>QSK19 Engines</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Front Crankshaft Seal</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3096478\">3096478</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3804703\">3804703</a></td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Dry)</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3096479\">3096479</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3804704\">3804704</a></td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Wet)</td><td>3090297</td><td>3090297</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td>3824971</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive (Fuel-Pump Side)</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3096480\">3096480</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3804705\">3804705</a></td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive(Water-Pump Side)</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3096480\">3096480</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3804705\">3804705</a></td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td></tr><tr><td><b>V28 Engines (Right-Hand Rotation)</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Front Crankshaft Seal</td><td>3020189</td><td>3020182</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST1304</td><td>-</td><td>3006744</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Dry)</td><td>3082142</td><td>3630681</td><td>3070080</td><td>-</td><td>ST1093</td><td>3824424</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Wet)</td><td>3001771</td><td>3005887</td><td>3076066</td><td>-</td><td>ST1093</td><td>3824424</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive(Fuel Pump Side)</td><td>3020187</td><td>3020187</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>3825104</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive (Water Pump Side)</td><td>3020190</td><td>3020190</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>3825104</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Generator Drive Housing</td><td>3020188</td><td>3020188</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>3825104</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td><b>V28 Engines (Left-Hand Rotation)</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Front Crankshaft Seal</td><td>3021095</td><td>3021096</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST1304</td><td>ST1304</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Dry)</td><td>3012542</td><td>3012544</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST1093</td><td>ST1093</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Wet)</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>ST1093</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive(Fuel-Pump Side)</td><td>3004316</td><td>3004316</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>3825104</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive (Water-Pump Side)</td><td>3020188</td><td>3020188</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>3825104</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Generator Drive Housing</td><td>3020190</td><td>3020190</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>3825104</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td><b>QST30 Engines</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Front Crankshaft Seal</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3016787\">3016787</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3016792\">3016792</a></td><td>3803994</td><td>-</td><td>3163485</td><td>3163485</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Dry)</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092821\">3092821</a></td><td>3099190</td><td>3099199</td><td>-</td><td>3825191</td><td>3825191</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Wet)</td><td>3092624</td><td>3099422</td><td>3099200</td><td>-</td><td>3825191 and 4918762</td><td>3825191 and 4918762</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive</td><td>3092812</td><td>3099197</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive (Water-Pump Side)</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092366\">3092366</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3099198\">3099198</a></td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Fuel-Pump Drive</td><td>3093304</td><td>3099196</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td><b>QSK38/50 andK38/50 Engines</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Front Crankshaft Seal</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3016787\">3016787</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3016792\">3016792</a>*</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>5298874</td><td>-</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Dry)</td><td>4396606</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3642365\">3642365</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3642365\">3642365</a></td><td>-</td><td>ST1093</td><td>3824424</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Wet)</td><td>3001771</td><td>3005887</td><td>3076066</td><td>-</td><td>ST1093</td><td>3824424</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive(Fuel-Pump Side)</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/5694571\">5694571</a></td><td>5573466</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/6378385\">6378385</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/6378385\">6378385</a></td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive(Water-Pump Side)</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/5694571\">5694571</a></td><td>5573466</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/6378385\">6378385</a></td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/6378385\">6378385</a></td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td><b>QSK45/60 Engines</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Front Crankshaft Seal</td><td>3171910</td><td>3171910</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Dry)</td><td>3171911</td><td>3171911</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td></tr><tr><td>Rear Crankshaft Seal (Wet)</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive(Fuel-Pump Side)</td><td>3171909</td><td>3171909</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td></tr><tr><td>Accessory Drive(Water-Pump Side)</td><td>3171909</td><td>3171909</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td><td><b>Not</b> Required</td></tr><tr><td>*See Technical Service Bulletin, Front Crankshaft Seal with Wear Sleeve and Press-On Shaft Excluder (POSE), <a class=\"lnk tsb\" href=\"#/doc/tsb120221\">TSB120221</a></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb101093":"<h2>New Water Pump O-ring Adapter</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This document announces the release of a new o-ring adapter for QSK38/50/60 MCRS water pumps. The new o-ring adapter obsoletes the previous part number. A dimensional change was made in the o-ring groove to improve the sealing properties of the joint at low temperatures.</p><p>This change was made to all dual impellor water pumps fitted to QSK38/50/60 MCRS engines, water pump options WP 6704, WP 6705, WP 6707, WP 6708, WP 6713, WP 6714, and WP 6718. The ESN first for this change was 33183776, built on November 8, 2010.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Previous O-ring Adapter Part Number</th><th>New O-ring Adapter Part Number</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>4951852</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3644172\">3644172</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08e00180.png\" alt=\"08e00180.png\"></figure><p>New O-ring Adapter, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3644172\">3644172</a></p><p>Number 1 points to the new adapter.</p><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb101094":"<h2>Temporary KV Rear Crankshaft Seal Tool</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>Recently a new rear crankhaft seal was released for use on K38/50 and QSK38/50 liter engines. The new seal required new tooling for installation and removal. The new tooling was unavailable at parts distribution centers when the seal was introduced. The following document instructs how to modify the current QSK45/60 crankshaft seal tool, Part Number 3163349, to enable it to install the new KV rear crankshaft seal.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>All the dimensions and measurements in this document are in millimeters.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00016.png\" alt=\"01s00016.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1, New adaptor plate (dimensions in mm)</p><p>Step 1 - Fabicate an adaptor plate as per the above drawing.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a short term solution until the new tool is readily available at parts distribution centers. The dimensions in the drawing below are in mm.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00017.png\" alt=\"01s00017.png\"></figure><p>Figure 2, QSK45/60 service tool, support modification</p><p>Step 2 - Modify the current QSK45/60 support and spacers.</p><ul><li>Elongate the support mounting holes (outwards) to the dimension shown</li><li>File the outer edges off the support; the outside diameter <b>must not</b> exceed 184 mm</li><li>Reduce the spacer height to 25 mm.</li></ul><p>Step 3 - Mount adaptor plate to QSK45/60 driver unit.</p><ul><li>The stepped edge faces away from the tool</li><li>Use 4 of M6x1x14 mm capscrews (Part Number 3900627)</li><li>Align the outside diameter of the adaptor plate with the outside diameter of the driver unit.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00018.png\" alt=\"01s00018.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00019.png\" alt=\"01s00019.png\"></figure><p>Figure 3, Installation of adaptor plate to QSK45/60 driver unit.</p><p>Step 4 - Seal Instllation.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01400080.png\" alt=\"01400080.png\"></figure><p>Make certain the crankshaft and flywheel housing seal mounting areas are clean.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00020.png\" alt=\"01s00020.png\"></figure><p>Place the seal on the crankshaft and lightly tap with a soft mallet to start the seal in place.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The seal part number is printed on the front face of the seal. The part number <b>must</b> face away from the cylinder block when installed.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00021.png\" alt=\"01s00021.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00022.png\" alt=\"01s00022.png\"></figure><p>Install the tool onto the crankshaft.</p><p>Make certain the support is centered on the crankshaft and clear of the seal.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00023.png\" alt=\"01s00023.png\"></figure><p>Install the driver unit on the support until it contacts the seal.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00024.png\" alt=\"01s00024.png\"></figure><p>Align the driver unit with the seal.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00025.png\" alt=\"01s00025.png\"></figure><p>Start to press the seal onto the crankshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00026.png\" alt=\"01s00026.png\"></figure><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>As the seal is pressed on, the driver can move slightly out of alignment with the seal. Make certain to realign the driver unit as it gets close to the crankshaft.</p></div></div><p>A small chamfer was added to the adapter to help guide the driver unit onto the crankshaft.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00027.png\" alt=\"01s00027.png\"></figure><p>Continue to press the seal into place until the adapter unit contacts the flywheel housing.</p><p>Approximate torque: 60 Nm [44 ft.lb.]</p><p>Make certain the seal driver unit is in full contact with the flywheel housing.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00028.png\" alt=\"01s00028.png\"></figure><p>Remove the driver unit and support from the crankshaft.</p><p>The seal will be pressed approximately 2 mm below the face of the flywheel housing.</p><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb101106":"<h2>Error 102 When Installing INSITE™ Electronic Service Tool 7.4.1 on Windows® Vista™/7 PCs</h2><h3>Core Issue</h3><p>Error 102 occurs when trying to install INSITE™ 7.4.1 with the Cummins® INSITE™ Update Manager.</p><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>This procedure should be followed after installing INSITE™ 7.4.1.</p><h3>Resolution</h3><p>NOTE: This procedure requires administrator rights to complete!!</p><ol><li>Download and save a copy of the MstFileReplaceUtility.zip to the desktop of the INSITE™ PC.</li><li>Unzip and extract the <b>MstFileReplaceUtility.exe</b> to the desktop of the INSITE™ PC.</li><li>Double-click the <b>MstFileReplaceUtility.exe</b> to run it.</li><li>The utility will give a message to confirm that the files were copied successfully. Click <b>OK</b> on this message.</li><li>Continue with the INSITE™ updates installation using the Cummins INSITE™ Update Manager.</li></ol><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb101121":"<h2>QST30 Only Runs on One Bank and Fault Code 166 is Active.</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>Issue:</p><p>When starting a QST30 engine it will activate fault 166 and <b>only</b> run on one bank if a voltage spike from the CM552 ECM is detected. When this occurs, the engine commonly runs on the right bank <b>only</b>.</p><p>Verification / Confirmation:</p><p>Confirm that Fault Code 166 is active and that the engine is <b>only</b> running on one bank.</p><p>Resolution:</p><p>A resistor has been added to the left bank engine wiring harness to prevent Fault Code 166 from becoming active and the engine from running on one bank if a voltage spike from the CM552 ECM occurs.</p><p>Check to see if there is a resistor installed between the rack position common wire and ground on the bank that is <b>not</b> firing. See the attached figures for resistor locations. If a resistor is <b>not</b> found, install a resistor in the wiring harness or replace the wiring harness. Refer to the wiring diagram for the pin location identification. If a resistor is found, check the resistance.</p><ul><li>For power generation applications, use the following procedure in the QST30 CM850 Power Generation Interface Engine Electronic Control System Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021674\">4021674</a>. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/60-019-043\">Refer to Procedure 019-043 in Section 19.</a></li><li>For industrial applications, use the following procedure in the QST30 Industrial Electronic Control System Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666214\">3666214</a> for resistance check instructions. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/87-019-043\">Refer to Procedure 019-043 in Section 19.</a></li></ul><p>The tables below summarize changes to the engine wiring harness:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th><b>QST30 CM552 Industrial One-Piece Harness Engines</b></th><th><b>Part Number</b></th><th><b>ESN First or Plant Implementation Date</b></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>One 2.2k Ohm Resistor (right bank <b>only</b>)</td><td>4975508</td><td>3-August-2009</td></tr><tr><td>Two 2.2k Ohm Resistors</td><td>4975755</td><td>37247268</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th><b>QST30 CM850 Power Generation Interface Engines</b></th><th><b>Part Number</b></th><th><b>ESN First or Plant Implementation Date</b></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>One 2.2k Ohm Resistor (right bank <b>only</b>)</td><td>4975505</td><td>25-May-2009</td></tr><tr><td>Two 2.2k Ohm Resistors with 12 Volt Fuel Pump Relay</td><td>2881121</td><td>13-December-2009</td></tr><tr><td>Two 2.2k Ohm Resistors with 24 Volt Fuel Pump Relay</td><td>4975747</td><td>37245679</td></tr><tr><td>Two 1.3k Ohm Resistors with 24 Volt Fuel Pump Relay</td><td>4975760</td><td>37246974</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19f00008.png\" alt=\"19f00008.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19f00009.png\" alt=\"19f00009.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19f00006.png\" alt=\"19f00006.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/19f00007.png\" alt=\"19f00007.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1: Resistor Location for QST30 Industrial Left Bank</p><p>Figure 2: Resistor Location for QST30 Industrial Right Bank</p><p>Figure 3: Resistor Location for QST30 Power Generation Interface Left Bank</p><p>Figure 4: Resistor Location for QST30 Power Generation Interface Right Bank</p><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb101122":"<h2>New K38/50 and QSK38/50 Jumper Covers and Jumper Cover Gasket</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00031.png\" alt=\"01s00031.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1: Jumper Cover Location</p><p>This document introduces a new jumper cover gasket and jumper covers for use on all K38, K50, QSK38, and QSK50 engines.</p><p>The jumper cover is also referred to as the oil transfer connection and its location on the engine is shown in Figure 1.</p><p>The jumper cover gasket material has been changed from steel core to edge molded to increase durability and reduce the potential for leaks.</p><p>Due to the new jumper cover gasket being slightly thicker, the jumper covers have been revised to prevent possible interference between the jumper cover and the engine starter motor.</p><p>The new jumper covers and gasket were released on December 20, 2010 for use in all K38, K50, QSK38 and QSK50 engines with ESN first 33184438.</p><h4>If a new, edge molded gasket is installed to an engine fitted with an old jumper cover, there is a possibility that there may be interference between the jumper cover and the starter. If there is an interference condition, there are two possible options:</h4><ul><li>The jumper cover can be machined so that 1.1 mm [0.043 inch] of material is machined off of the mating face of the cover. See Figure 4. After machining, the surface should have a flatness of 0.25 deviation and a surface finish of 3.2 roughness average, maximum.</li><li>The old jumper cover can be replaced with a new style cover.</li></ul><p>If there is no interference, an old style cover can be used with a new style gasket.</p><p>Do <b>not</b> remove material from the outer surface of the cover, as the reduced wall thickness could result in a malfunction of the cover.</p><h4>A jumper cover can be identified as old or new by either the part number, shown in the Table 1, or by measuring the cover thickness as follows:</h4><ul><li>There are six counter-bored holes used to attach the cover to the cylinder block.</li><li>Measure the thickness of the material between the bottom of the counter-bored hole and the machined face of the cover. See Figure 3.</li><li>An old cover will have a thickness (dimension X in Figure 4) of 12 ±0.38 mm [0.472 ±0.0149 in]</li><li>A new cover will have a thickness (dimension X in Figure 4) of 10.9 ±0.38 mm [0.429 ±0.0149 in]</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00032.png\" alt=\"01s00032.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00033.png\" alt=\"01s00033.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01s00034.png\" alt=\"01s00034.png\"></figure><p>Figure 2: Gasket (1) and Jumper Covers (2 and 3)</p><p>Figure 3: Jumper Cover Thickness Measurement</p><p>Figure 4: Material to be removed from mating face of cover</p><p>Table 1 contains old and new gasket and jumper cover part numbers.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1: Gasket and Jumper Cover Part Numbers</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Old Part Number</td><td>Material</td><td>New Part Number</td><td>Material</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Gasket</td><td>3627938</td><td>Steel Core</td><td>3642342</td><td>Edge Moulded</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Jumper Cover</td><td>3638576</td><td>n/a</td><td>3642472</td><td>n/a</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Jumper Cover</td><td>3629146</td><td>n/a</td><td>3642473</td><td>n/a</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>See the following procedure in the K38, K50, QSK38, and QSK50 Service Manual, Bulletin Number <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021528\">4021528</a>, for additional information on the lubricating oil jumper cover. <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/28-007-022-tr\">Refer to Procedure 007-022 in Section 7.</a></p><h3>Document History</h3>","tsb101140":"<h2>New Lubricating Oil Filter System</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This service/parts topic describes a redesign of the lubricating oil filtration system on the QST30 engine.</p><p>The old system consists of a full-flow filter head and a separate bypass filter head mounted in various locations on the engine. The full-flow filter head mounts four full-flow oil filters. The bypass filter head mounts two bypass oil filters. Filtered oil exiting the bypass filters is routed either to the number 6 right-bank cam follower cover or to the front cover where it drains to the oil pan.</p><p>The new lubricating oil filtration system was designed to utilize four Venturi Combo oil filters, Fleetguard® LF9001, Part Number 3406809. The LF9001 filters use patented technology to combine both full-flow and bypass filtration in a single filter. The new system consists of one Venturi Combo filter head, Part Number 3093596, that mounts four LF9001 filters. As a result, the bypass filter head and related components from the old system are <b>not</b> necessary.</p><p>The Venturi Combo filter head uses four replaceable adapters that are bolted to the head to provide the mounting point for the LF9001 filters. The old filter head uses adapters that are threaded into the head for filter mounting. It is <b>not</b> possible to mount the Venturi Combo adapters to the old full-flow filter head. However, the Venturi Combo filter head will mount directly in place of the old full-flow filter head. If this is done, the bypass filtration system can be removed.</p><p>The Venturi Combo lubricating oil filtration system offers several advantages over the old system. The primary advantage is the ability to extend oil and filter change intervals to 500 hours when Venturi Combo filters are used with premium grade engine oil. Premium grade oils meet API class CH4 specification, ACEA designation E5, and Cummins Engineering Standards 20071, 20072, and 20076. Valvoline® Premium Blue® oil meets all specifications to be classified as a premium grade oil. Use of Venturi Combo filters with standard grade oils requires an oil and filter change interval of 250 hours, or the use of the chart method with fuel consumption monitoring and oil sample analysis.</p><p>The LF9001 filter uses synthetic StrataPore™ media, which has the following benefits over cellulose media:</p><ul><li>Improved hot and cold flow</li><li>More consistent performance</li><li>Increased resistance to media rupture.</li></ul><p>The LF9001 filter uses an improved seal design, which is required with extended oil change intervals. The structural strength of the filter has been increased. Finally, the new system reduces the number of filters that are changed, reducing associated disposal costs.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div><ul><li>Order upfit kit, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4089094\">4089094</a>, which includes all parts necessary to convert an old system to the Venturi Combo system.</li><li>Remove the old filter head and replace with the Venturi Combo filter head. Replace the two grommets, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3093019\">3093019</a>, and two o-rings, Part Number 3092438, between the oil supply/return tubes and the filter head. Replace the two o-rings, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3093809\">3093809</a>, between the oil supply/return tubes and the oil transfer connection. Refer to Procedure 007-015 in the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, QST30 Series Engines, Bulletin 3666217.</li><li>Remove the bypass filter head, filter head bracket, and bypass oil supply and return hoses.</li><li>On power generation engines, plug the bypass oil supply line at the oil transfer connection and the oil return line to the number 6 right-bank cam follower cover with threaded plug, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3094340\">3094340</a>, and a sealing washer, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3094092\">3094092</a>.</li></ul><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>23 n•m [204 in-lb]</p></div></div><ul><li>On industrial engines, plug the return line to the front gear cover with a threaded plug and o-ring, Part Number <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3089238\">3089238</a>. The oil supply port on the Venturi Combo filter head comes with plugs installed.</li></ul><div class=\"callout tip\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">🔧</span>Момент затяжки · Torque Value</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>27 n•m [239 in-lb]</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07a00139.png\" alt=\"07a00139.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Venturi Combo Lubricating Oil Filter Head, Part Number 3093596</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Item Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Description</td><td>Quantity</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>3093562</td><td>Lubricating filter head</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3678924\">3678924</a></td><td>Threaded plug</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3678925\">3678925</a></td><td>O-ring</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3094129\">3094129</a></td><td>O-ring (1 shown)</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>3094040</td><td>Cover plate (no ports)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3335076\">3335076</a></td><td>Bevel washer (1 shown)</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3093744\">3093744</a></td><td>Hex head capscrew (1 shown)</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>200819</td><td>Bypass disc (1 shown)</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092078\">3092078</a></td><td>Spring (1 shown)</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3094836\">3094836</a></td><td>Sealing washer (1 shown)</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3094042\">3094042</a></td><td>Threaded plug (1 shown)</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3090126\">3090126</a></td><td>O-ring (1 shown)</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3090127\">3090127</a></td><td>O-ring (1 shown)</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>3092967</td><td>Filter head adapter (1 shown)</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3925402\">3925402</a></td><td>Hex flange head capscrew (1 shown)</td><td>16</td></tr><tr><td>N/A*</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092582\">3092582</a></td><td>Cover plate (3 ports)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>N/A*</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3089238\">3089238</a></td><td>Threaded plug (Use with <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092582\">3092582</a>)</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>N/A*</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3678921\">3678921</a></td><td>Threaded plug (Use with <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092582\">3092582</a>)</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>*N/A indicates <b>not</b> applicable.</p>","tsb101150":"<h2>Fuel Inlet Check Valve and 10 Micron Fuel Filter</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This service/parts topic provides information on the improved fuel filtration capability and updates procedure 018-024.</p><p>Improved fuel filtration capability has been introduced for the QST30 industrial engines. Industrial engines are now using Fleetguard FS1006 filters, Cummins Part Number 3089916. The FS1006 offers 10 micron [.0004 in] filtration and water separation capability, and will mount to the existing filter head on all QST30 engines. The FS1006 is a direct replacement for the FF202 filters used previously.</p><p>When the water drain valve on the bottom of the filter is opened, a drain-back path exists for fuel to return to the tank when the tank fuel level is below filter level. This condition introduces air into the supply lines, and could result in hard starting. Drainback could also occur if there was any air leaks into the fuel system.</p><p>A check valve has been added at the fuel inlet manifold, to reduce the possibility of drain-back. The check valve includes a 300 micron filter screen inside the fitting. The filter screen can be removed for cleaning by isolating the fuel tank, disconnecting the fuel supply hose, and removing the fitting from the check valve. The check valve remains in the fuel manifold to reduce the possibility of fuel from draining out of the engine. The screen is then removed from the fitting for cleaning.</p><p>In the event of a low power complaint or the presence of Fault Code 423 or 423R, the filter screen should be inspected for debris.</p><p>A 27.6 kPa [4 psi] banjo check valve relieves pressure from the supply to the drain, to reduce the possibility of fuel filter seal damage due to fuel expansion after shutdown. This check valve is mounted on top of the fuel manifold on the supply side.</p><p>Engine serial number first for Euclid engines with the fuel inlet check valve and FS1006 fuel filters is 37198242, built on 16 April 2001. Engine serial number first for Komatsu engines is 37202119, built on 28 January 2002. Engine serial number first for all other OEM&#x27;S IS 37200921, built on 15 October 2001.</p><p>A kit is available to upfit QST30 Industrial engines built prior to the engine serial number first listed above. The kit part number is 4089113. In addition to the kit, it is also necessary to order the appropriate fuel manifold for the engine. The fuel manifold required is based on the FT (Fuel Tubing) option the engine uses. The fuel tubing option content is:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Manifold</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>FT5709</td><td>4067988</td></tr><tr><td>All others</td><td>4067987</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The fuel manifold is <b>not</b> included with the upfit kit and <b>must</b> be ordered separately.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/06a00123.png\" alt=\"06a00123.png\"></figure><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Fuel Filter Upfit Kit Part Numbers</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Reference Number</td><td>Part Number</td><td>Quantity</td><td>Description</td><td>Torque</td></tr><tr><td>Not shown</td><td>3089916</td><td>2</td><td>Filter, fuel (FS1006)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3094188\">3094188</a></td><td>1</td><td>Bolt, banjo</td><td>7 N•m [62 in-lb]</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3918188\">3918188</a></td><td>2</td><td>Washer, sealing (M8)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>4067979</td><td>1</td><td>Tube, fuel by-pass</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4067813\">4067813</a></td><td>1</td><td>Fitting, fuel drain</td><td>80 N•m [59 ft-lb]</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>4067950</td><td>1</td><td>Fitting, fuel supply</td><td>80 N•m [59 ft-lb]</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>2918190</td><td>2</td><td>Washer, sealing (M10)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>4067977</td><td>1</td><td>Check valve, banjo</td><td>11 N•m [97 in-lb]</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb101210":"<h2>Engine Datalinks</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This service/parts topic supersedes topic 99T19-6 and topic 99T19-6A; replace 99T19-6 and 99T19-6A with this one. This procedure describes connecting engine datalinks to electronic service tools. This procedure provides a list of the contents of the INLINE™, INLINE™ I and INLINE™ II datalink kits. It also describes datalink adapters, datalink connectors, and connecting to an Electronic Control Module (ECM).</p>","tsb101364":"<h2>Centinel™ Feature Update</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Centinel™ Feature.</p>","tsb101365":"<h2>Centinel™ System Description</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates the System Description (209-001) of the Centinel™ Master Repair Manual.</p>","tsb101519":"<h2>New General Cleaning Instruction</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic is a revision to Procedure <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/99-204-008\">204-008</a> for General Cleaning Instructions.</p><p>Considerable concern has been generated at both the factory and the field about engine failures that occur a short time after an in-frame repair. Analysis of returned parts indicates many of the failures are the result of dirt entering the engine during the repair. In particular, intensive investigation of failures of ISX engines rod and main bearings very soon after field repairs of the oil coolers, front gear cover, or cylinder head has shown that 30 percent of the failures are due to contamination of some main oil drillings. Investigation into the type and source of the contamination indicates it is appropriate to remind, review, and revise parts cleaning instructions for all engines.</p><p>The statement &#x27;A person can spend too much time cleaning parts but a person can <b>not</b> get them too clean&#x27; is even more relevant as customer expectations and regulatory requirements increase. These demands coupled with increased diesel engine product complexity place more pressure on the field technician in terms of time required to perform a quality repair. In a effort to reduce customer downtime, many different labor saving devices, techniques, and shortcuts are being used to meet customer expectations. However, some of the shortcuts and labor saving efforts are the very things that can cause contamination of internal engine components that lead to additional failures.</p><p>Attached is the revised General Cleaning Instructions that will be placed in all service publications where those instructions are included. Field shops are strongly encouraged to review these instructions with all technicians and to include general cleaning instructions in technician training programs and new technician orientation programs.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb101572":"<h2>Fuel Shutoff Valve Solenoid Resistance Specification</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to notify the field of a change in electrical resistance specifications for the fuel shutoff valve solenoid. The new resistance specifications are more accurate than the old specifications. The new specifications are listed in the table below.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Revised Fuel System Shutoff Valve Solenoid Specifications</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Voltage</td><td>Resistance Minimum (Ohms)</td><td>Resistance Maximum (Ohms)</td></tr><tr><td>6 VDC</td><td>1</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>12 VDC</td><td>6</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>24 VDC</td><td>24</td><td>50</td></tr><tr><td>32 VDC</td><td>42</td><td>80</td></tr><tr><td>36 VDC</td><td>46</td><td>87</td></tr><tr><td>48 VDC</td><td>92</td><td>145</td></tr><tr><td>74 VDC</td><td>315</td><td>375</td></tr><tr><td>115 VAC</td><td>645</td><td>735</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>In all cases the solenoid terminals <b>must</b> be thoroughly cleaned before the measurement is taken. In the case of the single pole solenoids, it is recommended to scrape paint off another portion of the solenoid cast iron housing. Good contact pressure with the multimeter terminals is recommended as well as a stable measurement on the display before the reading is compared against the specifications.</p><p>Fault Code 254 and Fault Code 259 are being updated to reflect the new specifications.</p>","tsb101586":"<h2>New Oil Suction Tube Bracket</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts topic introduces a new oil suction tube bracket for the QST30 Industrial engines.</p><p>The existing bracket is a singular column of angled iron shown in Figure 1 and will continue to be used on Power Generation engines. The new Industrial bracket is triangular in shape and is shown in Figure 2.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07a00141.png\" alt=\"07a00141.png\"></figure><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07a00142.png\" alt=\"07a00142.png\"></figure><p>Figure 1, Existing Singular Column Bracket</p><p>Figure 2, New Triangular Shaped Bracket</p><p>The repair procedures will <b>not</b> change.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Existing Part Number</th><th>New Part Number</th><th>Quantity</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3094397</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/4068734\">4068734</a></td><td>1</td><td>Bracket, oil tube</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb101647":"<h2>Cummins/Fleetguard® Filter Specifications Update</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates the Cummins/Fleetguard® Filter Specifications procedure to include the no water separation fuel prefilter.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb101822":"<h2>Two Pump, Two Loop Cooling System Diagram</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds an exploded view to Procedure 100-002, with the two pump, two loop cooling system configuration.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/08a00192.png\" alt=\"08a00192.png\"></figure><p>Non-Thermostatically Controlled Two Pump Two Loop Cooling System</p><ol><li>Low temperature aftercooled water pump inlet</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water pump</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water pump support bracket</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water transfer hose</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water transfer hose</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water transfer connection</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water inlet transfer hose</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water inlet transfer hose</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water outlet transfer hose</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water inlet transfer hose</li><li>Low temperature aftercooled water outlet.</li></ol>","tsb101850":"<h2>QST30 Tier 2 Engine Introduction</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This Service/Parts Topic supersedes and replaces Service/Parts Topics 97t0-7 and 99t0-22.</p></div></div><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces the introduction of the QST30 Tier 2, Tier 1, non-certified products, and identifies unique engine components for the non-certified products.</p><p>The QST30 Tier 2 engine is redesigned to address the US Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) exhaust emissions levels for off-highway engines in the &gt;560 kW [&gt;751 HP] power category built after 01 January 2006. It is built to meet and exceed present and future competitive pressures, worldwide emissions regulations, and corporate standards for performance, reliability and durability.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QST30 Tier 2 Industrial</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Configuration Number</td><td>D573002CX03</td><td>D573003CX03</td></tr><tr><td>Number of Cylinders</td><td>12</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Displacement</td><td>30.5 liters [1860 in 3 ]</td><td>30.5 liters [1861 in 3 ]</td></tr><tr><td>Bore</td><td>140 mm [5.51 in]</td><td>140 mm [5.51 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Stroke</td><td>165 mm [6.5 in]</td><td>165 mm [6.5 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Compression Ratio</td><td>15.7:1</td><td>14.7:1</td></tr><tr><td>Aspiration</td><td>Turbocharged and Charge Air Cooled</td><td>Turbocharged and 2-Pump 2-Loop Aftercooled</td></tr><tr><td>Approximate Engine Weight</td><td>3328 kg [7337 lbs]</td><td>3328 kg [7337 lbs]</td></tr><tr><td>Maximum Overspeed Capacity</td><td>2625 rpm</td><td>2625 rpm</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QST30 Tier 2 Power Generation</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Configuration Number</td><td>D573001GX03</td></tr><tr><td>Number of Cylinders</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Displacement</td><td>30.5 liters [1860 in 3 ]</td></tr><tr><td>Bore</td><td>140 mm [5.51 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Stroke</td><td>165 mm [6.5 in]</td></tr><tr><td>Compression Ratio</td><td>14.7:1</td></tr><tr><td>Aspiration</td><td>Turbocharged and Charge Air Cooled, 2-Pump 2-Loop Aftercooled, Jacket Water Aftercooled</td></tr><tr><td>Approximate Engine Weight</td><td>3112 kg [6860 lbs]</td></tr><tr><td>Maximum Overspeed Capacity</td><td>2625 rpm</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>QST30 Tier 2 Engine Ratings (Industrial)</p><p>The fuel ratings available for the QST30 Tier 2 engine are essentially a carryover from the QST30 Tier 1 engine. The performance parts have been developed to meet Tier 2 emission levels, achieve the best possible fuel consumption, and achieve similar transient response as the Tier 1 engine.</p><p>The Tier 2 ratings shown below are planned for production availability. Additional ratings, performance curves, and data sheets are available and can be obtained at a Cummins Authorized Service Location.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QST30 Configuration Number - D573002CX03</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Option Number</td><td>CPL Number</td><td>Power kW [bhp] @ rpm</td><td>Peak Torque N•m [ft-lb] @ rpm</td><td>Rating Type</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5234</td><td>1244</td><td>895 [1200] @ 2100</td><td>5084 [3750] @ 1400</td><td>Restricted</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5235</td><td>1244</td><td>895 [1200] @ 1900</td><td>5085 [3751] @ 1400</td><td>Restricted</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5236</td><td>1244</td><td>820 [1100] @ 2100</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1400</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5237</td><td>1244</td><td>783 [1050] @ 2100</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5239</td><td>1244</td><td>783 [1050] @ 1900</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5238</td><td>1244</td><td>783 [1050] @ 1800</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5240</td><td>1244</td><td>746 [1000] @ 2100</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5241</td><td>1244</td><td>746 [1000] @ 1800</td><td>4629 [3414] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5242</td><td>1244</td><td>708 [950] @ 2100</td><td>4188 [3089] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5243</td><td>1244</td><td>671 [900] @ 2100</td><td>3747 [2764] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5244</td><td>1244</td><td>634 [850] @ 2000</td><td>3806 [2807] @ 1400</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5245</td><td>1244</td><td>634 [850] @ 1800</td><td>3806 [2807] @ 1400</td><td>Continuous</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5246</td><td>1244</td><td>567 [760] @ 2100</td><td>3350 [2471] @ 1300</td><td>Intermittent</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Engine Ratings (Power Generation)</p><p>The fuel ratings available for the QST30 Tier 2 engine are essentially a carryover from the QST30 Tier 1 engine. The performance parts have been developed to meet Tier 2 emission levels, achieve the best possible fuel consumption, and achieve similar transient response as the Tier 1 engine. The QST30 Tier 2 ratings shown in the table below are planned for production availability. Additional ratings can be requested by submitting a Value Package Change Request (VPCR). Additional ratings, performance curves, and data sheets are available and can be obtained at a Cummins Authorized Service Location.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th></th><th></th><th>Standby</th><th>Prime</th><th>Continuous</th><th>Cooling</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td></td><td></td><td>1500</td><td>1800</td><td>1500</td><td>1800</td><td>1500</td><td>1800</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td>HP/KWm</td><td>HP/KWm</td><td>HP/KWm</td><td>HP/KWm</td><td>HP/KWm</td><td>HP/KWm</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>FR 5247</td><td>QST30-G5 NR2</td><td>N/A</td><td>1490/1112</td><td>N/A</td><td>1350/1007</td><td>N/A</td><td>1115/832</td><td>2P2L</td></tr><tr><td>FR 5250</td><td>QST30-G5 NR2</td><td>N/A</td><td>1490/1112</td><td>N/A</td><td>1350/1007</td><td>N/A</td><td>1115/832</td><td>ATA</td></tr><tr><td>Additional ratings, performance curves, and data sheets are available and can be obtained at a Cummins Authorized Service Location.</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The QST30 Industrial Tier 1 service parts topic introduced the Tier 1 emission-certified QST30 engine for mobile off-highway applications. A new procedure for the charge-air cooler (CAC), a new symptom tree, and revisions to five other symptom trees were also included in the Tier 1 engine introduction.</p><p>To meet year 2000 Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) and California Air Resources Board (CARB) Tier 1 emission levels, it was necessary to change the non-certified QST30 aspiration from turbocharged and jacket water aftercooled (JWAC) to turbocharged and charge-air cooled (CAC). The Tier 1 product employs two separate cooling circuits; A liquid-coolant-filled high-temperature circuit (HTC) for the main engine jacket water cooling, and a low-temperature, air-to-air circuit (LTC) for charge-air cooling. This topic addressed <b>only</b> the differences between the Tier 1 and non-certified QST30 Industrial engines.</p><p>Charge-air cooling of the intake air was required to retain engine efficiency while injection timing was retarded to obtain lower NOx. Charge-air cooling also allowed higher horsepower capabilities for the equivalent thermal loading. In addition to the non-certified QST30 power ranges of 760 hp to 1050 hp, a 1200 hp with 6000-foot altitude capability became available. The new offering also featured a 25 percent torque rise and is restricted to intermittent applications with load factors equal to or less than 40 percent.</p><p>QST30 Industrial Tier 1 limited production began 01 January 2000 and retained the configuration number D573002CX03.</p><p>For general charge-air cooling installation guidelines, see the Application Engineering Bulletin Number 3884966, (AEB) 24.06 - 1999 Industrial Application Installation Recommendations, Charge-Air Cooling.</p><p>Emission Regulations</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Year 2000 Tier 1 Emission Regulations</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Emission Regulating Agency</td><td>Emission Limit (g/bhp-hr) NOx</td><td>Horsepower</td></tr><tr><td>CARB</td><td>6.9 NOx</td><td>Above 750 hp</td></tr><tr><td>EPA</td><td>6.9 NOx</td><td>Above 750 hp</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Ratings</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The <b>only</b> difference between CPL 2640 and CPL 2818 is the orientation of the turbocharger compressor housings. The base turbocharger part number is the same for the two CPLs.</p></div></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QST30 Industrial Tier 1 Ratings</th><th></th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Engine Model</td><td>Rated Horsepower kW [bhp] rpm, N•m [ft-lb] rpm</td><td>Application</td><td>CPL</td><td>ECM Code</td></tr><tr><td>QST30-C</td><td>669 [897]@2000 rpm. Torque peak: 4103 [3026]@1300 rpm</td><td>Komatsu WA900, front-out exhaust</td><td>2640</td><td>K50017</td></tr><tr><td>QST30-C</td><td>807 [897]@2000 rpm. Torque peak: 4629 [3414]@1400 rpm</td><td>Komatsu 330M, rear-out exhaust, with PMC, with CENSE™</td><td>2818</td><td>K50019</td></tr><tr><td>QST30-C</td><td>567 [760]@2100 rpm. Torque peak: 3350 [2471]@1300 rpm</td><td>Kawasaki 135Z</td><td>2640</td><td>K50018</td></tr><tr><td>Additional ratings, performance curves, and data sheets are available and can be obtained at a Cummins Authorized Service Location.</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The QST30-C Industrial service parts topic announced the introduction of the QST30-C Industrial engine.</p><p>New industrial ratings of the QST30 engine were released for limited production in September, 1997. Four ratings of this industrial engine were released. The QST30-C uses many of the successfully proven technologies already in production on QST30 Power Generation engines. The QST30-C uses a full-authority electronic Bosch® fuel system, Cummins Inc. developed controls, and is fully compatible with the CENSE™ engine monitoring system. QST30-C Industrial ratings are designed to replace V28 and lower K38 ratings with improved fuel economy, transient response, emissions, and diagnostic capabilities.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>QST30-C Non-Certified Industrial</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Model Name</td><td>QST30-1050</td></tr><tr><td>Configuration Number</td><td>D573002CX03</td></tr><tr><td>CPL</td><td>2127</td></tr><tr><td>Fuel Code</td><td>105</td></tr><tr><td>Injector (Qty.)</td><td>3092022 (2), 3092023 (10)</td></tr><tr><td>Crankshaft</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092922\">3092922</a></td></tr><tr><td>Camshft (Qty.)</td><td><a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092971\">3092971</a> (1), <a class=\"lnk part\" href=\"#/part/3092974\">3092974</a> (1).</td></tr><tr><td>Piston (Qty.)</td><td>3092606 (6), 3092607, (6).</td></tr><tr><td>Turbocharger (Qty.)</td><td>3537114 (1), 3097115 (1).</td></tr><tr><td>Cylinder Head</td><td>3094190</td></tr><tr><td>Horsepower</td><td>1050 hp @ 2100 rpm</td></tr><tr><td>Torque</td><td>3415 ft-lb @ 1300 rpm</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The QST30-C Industrial engine contains several unique parts. A general description of these components and a listing of parts that are not shared with the power generation QST30 engines. Components are organized by group for ease of use.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The QST30-C engines used in Komatsu applications will be Komatsu branded and designated SA12V140 Z-1. They will <b>not</b> be Cummins Inc. labeled or identified as QST30-C. The engines in Komatsu applications are <b>not</b> covered by Cummins Inc. warranty, and they will be serviced through the Komatsu service network.</p></div></div>","tsb102004":"<h2>New Fault Codes 772 and 773</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces Fault Codes 772 and 773 for the QST30 engine.</p>","tsb103229":"<h2>Procedure 006-026 (Injector), Replace Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the Procedure 006-026 (Injector) to Section 10 of the Operation and Maintenance Manual K38, K50, QSK38 and QSK50, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3810497\">3810497</a>. This procedure recommends injector replacement at engine half life to rebuild for both the mechanically and electronically actuated injectors.</p>","tsb103619":"<h2>Fault Code 2727, Guided Step 2D Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds Guided Step 2D to Fault Code 2727, in Section TF of the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual QSK38, QSK50 and QSK60 CM850 Modular Common Rail System, Bulletin 4021533.</p>","tsb103816":"<h2>New Lift Pump</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a new lift pump for the QST30 engine and supersedes Service/Parts Topic 09T5-4.</p><p>The new lift pump has a hardened gerotor with an improved tolerance for debris. The new lift pump, Part Number 4975617, went into production with engine serial number (ESN) First 37240363.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Old Part Number</th><th>New Part Number</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>4975518</td><td>4975617</td><td>PUMP, FUEL TRANSFER</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb103985":"<h2>Camshaft Gear (Camshaft Installed) Procedure, Initial Check and Measure Section Additions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds Initial Check and Measure section to Procedure 001-012 (Camshaft Gear (Camshaft Installed) in the K38, K50, QSK38, and QSK50 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021528\">4021528</a>.</p>","tsb104027":"<h2>Cylinder Liner Procedure, Clean and Inspect for Reuse and Measure Section Revision; Piston Rings Procedure, Measure Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedures 001-028 (Cylinder Liner) and 001-047 (Piston Rings). A new top piston ring resulted in the piston ring gap clearances being different than the original ring. The modifications to the piston rings include new details of the new clearance, as well as introduce a specific region on the liner bore which will be used for this measurement. The changes to the cylinder liner procedure are associated with the piston ring procedure in that it asks for the cylinder liner to be measured in the same region as the piston ring. It requires the diameter at this point to be recorded so it can be used to assist in the assessment of the piston ring gap in the piston ring procedure.</p><p>Procedure 001-028 (Cylinder Liner), Measure Section, used in the Engine Assembly Section of Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021528\">4021528</a>, did <b>not</b> include a section on how to measure the cylinder liner protrusion. A link has been placed at the end of the Measure Section, directing users to Procedure 001-064 (Cylinder Liner Protrusion).</p>","tsb104031":"<h2>Eliminator™ Filter Procedure, Disassembly and Assembly Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Disassemble and Assemble Sections of Procedure 007-067 (Eliminator™ Filter), to add reference to the centrifuge spindle (item 49) removal and installation. A torque specification for the spindle (item 49) has been added to the Assemble Section.</p>","tsb104078":"<h2>Water Pump and LTA Water Pump Procedures, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 008-062 (Water Pump) and Procedure 008-109 (Low-Temperature Aftercooler (LTA) Water Pump)) in Section 8 in Service Manual, K38, K50, QSK38, and QSK50, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021528\">4021528</a>. The Mechanically Actuated Injector sections have been renamed to Jacket and the Electronically Actuated Injector sections have been renamed to Dual Impeller. The Mechanically Actuated Injector section name was removed from Procedure 008-109 in Section 8.</p>","tsb104105":"<h2>New Fuel Filter Procedures</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises procedure Fuel Filter (Spin-On Type), dividing the information into three separate procedures:</p><ul><li>Procedure 006-015 (Fuel Filter (Spin-On Type)) is for the fuel filter on engines with mechanically actuated injectors.</li><li>Procedure 006-075 (Fuel Filter Stage 1) is for the stage 1 filter on engines with electronically actuated injectors.</li><li>Procedure 006-076 (Fuel Filter Stage 2) is for the stage 2 filter on engines with electronically actuated injectors.</li></ul>","tsb104112":"<h2>Maintenance Schedule Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces revisions to the Maintenance Schedule. The Eliminator™ Filter Rotation Check should now be performed at the Daily interval and the Eliminator™ Filter Pressure Check should now be performed at the 1,000 hour/1 year interval.</p>"};
